IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-1`
IMPORT `spr-part8-credits-2`

-- Tests for regulations 29 to 33 (spr-part8-credits-2.l4).
-- Expected values are decided from the text of the regulation named beside each
-- group, before running. Tax years are named by the calendar year they start in (F3).

§ `Fixtures for regulation 33 (the same facts as regulation 28)`
`forces spouse, week of 7 Jun 2010, all in order` MEANS ForcesSpouseFacts WITH
    `the first day of the week` IS YMD 2010 6 7
    `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation` IS TRUE
    `the person is accompanying the member of Her Majesty's forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
    `the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty's forces for the year` IS 12000
    `the qualifying earnings factor for the year` IS 5000
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `an application to be credited has been received by the Secretary of State` IS TRUE
    `the application is made in respect of a past period` IS TRUE
    `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient` IS TRUE
    `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` IS TRUE

