§ `Regulation 29: credits under the 1975 Regulations carry over`

#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 7 (credits for approved training)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 7A (credits for carer's allowance or carer support payment)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 7B (credits for disability element of working tax credit)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 8A (credits for unemployment)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 9C (credits for maternity pay etc.)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 9D (credits for certain periods of imprisonment or detention in legal custody)`
#ASSERT `regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces)`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 29(2): the provision is one the regulation specifies` `another provision of the 1975 Regulations`)
#ASSERT `regulation 29(1): the person is also credited for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act` `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 29(1): the person is also credited for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act` `regulation 9B (credits for jury service)` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 29(1): the person is also credited for the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act` `another provision of the 1975 Regulations` TRUE)

§ `Fixtures for regulation 30`
`employed earner paid working tax credit, LEL 123` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`low-profit self-employed earner paid working tax credit` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `a self-employed earner whose profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act, who would otherwise ... be treated as having actually paid, a Class 2 contribution`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`person excepted by regulation 43 paid working tax credit` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `a person excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`another kind of person paid working tax credit` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `another kind of person`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`working tax credit not paid for the week` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS FALSE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`entitled to credits under the 1975 Regulations` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS TRUE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`woman with a reduced rate election in force` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS FALSE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS TRUE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`couple, only one member assessed, and that is the person` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS TRUE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS TRUE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS TRUE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`couple, only one member assessed, and that is the other member` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS TRUE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS TRUE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS TRUE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`couple, both assessed, and the credit is paid to the person` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS TRUE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS TRUE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

`couple, both assessed, and the credit is paid to the other member` MEANS WorkingTaxCreditFacts WITH
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of the week` IS TRUE
    `the kind of person the person is in the week` IS `an employed earner`
    `working tax credit is paid in respect of a couple` IS TRUE
    `only one member of the couple is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS FALSE
    `the person is the member of the couple who is assessed as having income consisting of earnings` IS TRUE
    `the person is the member of the couple to whom working tax credit is paid` IS FALSE
    `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings for the week under regulation 7B, 8A or 8B of the 1975 Regulations` IS FALSE
    `the person is a woman for whom an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force for any part of the week` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123


§ `Regulation 30`

#ASSERT `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `employed earner paid working tax credit, LEL 123`
#ASSERT `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `low-profit self-employed earner paid working tax credit`
#ASSERT `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `person excepted by regulation 43 paid working tax credit`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `another kind of person paid working tax credit`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `working tax credit not paid for the week`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `entitled to credits under the 1975 Regulations`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `woman with a reduced rate election in force`)
-- (2): couples.
#ASSERT `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `couple, only one member assessed, and that is the person`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `couple, only one member assessed, and that is the other member`)
#ASSERT `regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `couple, both assessed, and the credit is paid to the person`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30: the person is credited with earnings for the week` `couple, both assessed, and the credit is paid to the other member`)
-- (3): the exclusions, separately.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 30(3): paragraph (1) does not apply` `employed earner paid working tax credit, LEL 123`)
#ASSERT `regulation 30(3): paragraph (1) does not apply` `entitled to credits under the 1975 Regulations`
#ASSERT `regulation 30(3): paragraph (1) does not apply` `woman with a reduced rate election in force`
-- The credit is earnings equal to the lower earnings limit then in force.
#ASSERT `regulation 30(1): the earnings credited` `employed earner paid working tax credit, LEL 123` EQUALS JUST 123
#ASSERT `regulation 30(1): the earnings credited` `another kind of person paid working tax credit` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `regulation 30(1): the earnings credited` `woman with a reduced rate election in force` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 31`

#ASSERT `regulation 31: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 31: the person is credited with a Class 3 contribution for the week` FALSE)

§ `Fixtures for regulation 32`
`man born 5 Oct 1953, week of 3 Oct 2016 (tax year 2016)` MEANS ApproachingPensionableAgeFacts WITH
    `the man's date of birth` IS YMD 1953 10 5
    `the date the man attains the age which is pensionable age in the case of a woman born on the same day` IS YMD 2016 1 5
    `the first day of the week` IS YMD 2016 10 3
    `the number of days the man is absent from Great Britain during the year` IS 0
    `the man is a self-employed earner` IS FALSE
    `the man would be treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution but for the fact that his profits for the year are below the small profits threshold specified by section 11(4)(b) of the 1992 Act` IS FALSE
    `the man is excepted from being treated as having actually paid a Class 2 contribution by virtue of regulation 43 of the Social Security (Contributions) Regulations 2001 in respect of any week in a year to which regulation 32 applies` IS FALSE
    `the lower earnings limit then in force in respect of the week` IS 123

